Wow, I was hoping to get in with some advice here, but it looks like
everyone's practically covered everything.

A few things they haven't mentioned:

Try to not drink potions and read scrolls if you don't know what they
are. Several of them can be quite dangerous, so it's best to wait and
either use methods of identification, or use them in a locked room.

The Mines are a good source of useful items, such as candles (you'll
find out why later, but make sure you've got seven), tools and
pickaxes. On top of that, it also contains Mine Town, what would be an
effective "home-base" if not for its depth in the mines. Regardless,
it has several useful facilities that'll certainly assist you. Just be
careful, the Mines are also a good source of stupid deaths (YASDs), so
if you do attempt them, make sure you're careful, have high AC and you
don't do anything you shouldn't do.

A rather important thing that I don't think has been mentioned is
fountains and sinks. Both can produce particularly nasty effects, and
fountains have killed many an early player. Stay away from them until,
say, Xp:5. They're dangerous for a bit past that, so if someone wants
to suggest a better level restriction, feel free.

I'm assuming you don't want to be spoiled?

